          <div class="section-label">Complete Buyer's Guide</div>
          <h2 id="guide-heading">Everything You Need to Know About Buying a Home in Hermosa Beach CA 90254</h2>
          <p>Hermosa Beach is one of those rare coastal communities where the phrase "quality of life" is not marketing language — it is the lived reality of 18,000 residents who have chosen one of the most desirable zip codes in the country. With three distinct neighborhoods ranging from accessible East Hermosa condos to multi-million dollar Strand properties, 90254 offers real options at different price points — as long as you understand what each part of the market actually requires from a financing standpoint.</p>
          <h3 id="why-hermosa">Why People Choose Hermosa Beach</h3>
          <p>Hermosa Beach sits between Manhattan Beach to the north and Redondo Beach to the south — and it has a quality that is difficult to quantify but instantly recognizable: it feels like a genuine small town. Pier Avenue's restaurants, shops, and community events. The South Bay Bicycle Trail along The Strand. The beach volleyball courts that have made Hermosa internationally recognized. A tight-knit resident community that participates actively in city life.</p>
          <p>From an investment perspective, Hermosa Beach real estate has demonstrated long-term appreciation that reflects permanent scarcity. The city is fully built out — there is no land for new development. This supply constraint, combined with consistent demand from buyers seeking coastal lifestyle in one of the most pleasant climates on earth, has supported values through economic cycles.</p>
          <h3 id="financing-hermosa">Financing in Hermosa Beach — The Jumbo Reality</h3>
          <p>The 2025 conforming loan limit for LA County is $1,209,750. With a median home value in 90254 of approximately $2.2M and a median SFR price of $2.8M, the vast majority of Hermosa Beach transactions require loan amounts well above the conforming limit. Here is what buyers need to know:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Credit score:</strong> Most jumbo lenders want 700+, with the best rates at 720+. Some programs accept 680 with compensating factors.</li>
            <li><strong>Down payment:</strong> Standard jumbo requires 20% down. On a $2.5M purchase, that is $500,000 in down payment plus $60,000–$80,000 in closing costs.</li>
            <li><strong>Reserves:</strong> Most jumbo programs require 12 months of PITI in verified liquid assets after closing — on a $2M+ loan, that is typically $150,000–$250,000 or more.</li>
            <li><strong>Self-employed buyers:</strong> Bank statement programs are available at the jumbo level for business owners whose tax returns understate qualifying income.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 id="schools-hermosa">Schools and Community</h3>
          <p>Hermosa Beach City School District serves K–8, with high school students attending Mira Costa High School in Manhattan Beach Unified — consistently ranked in the top 1–2% of California public high schools. The school community is tight-knit and deeply engaged, and school quality is a meaningful factor in Hermosa Beach home values.</p>
          <h3 id="next-steps-hermosa">Your Next Step</h3>
          <p>Whether you're eyeing the Tree Section, The Strand, or an East Hermosa entry point — the path starts with a jumbo pre-approval. Call me at (310) 594-5362 or fill out the form below. Free, 20 minutes, and I'll tell you exactly what it takes to buy in Hermosa Beach today.</p>
